<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;EMMANUEL DE SAINTE-HERMINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emmanuel de Sainte-Hermine was a French politician and Catholic priest who held various positions including desservant and member of the Chamber of Peers, known for his advocacy for the Catholic Church and his commitment to the faith and community."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH REVOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The French Revolution was a period of radical social and political upheaval in France, during which Sainte-Hermine became a vocal advocate for the rights of the Catholic Church."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAPOLEON BONAPARTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Napoleon Bonaparte was a French military and political leader who appointed Sainte-Hermine to several positions, including the Council of State and Prefect of the Seine-et-Oise department."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COUNCIL OF STATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Council of State was a body of advisors to the French monarch, where Sainte-Hermine served after the French Revolution."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAMBER OF PEERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Chamber of Peers was the upper house of the French parliament during the Bourbon Restoration, where Sainte-Hermine played a significant role in shaping French politics."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL CONVENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The National Convention was the legislative body of France during the early stages of the French Revolution, where Sainte-Hermine served as a deputy."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GIRONDIN FACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Girondin faction was a political group during the French Revolution, which Sainte-Hermine aligned himself with, advocating for a constitutional monarchy."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KING LOUIS XVIII&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"King Louis XVIII was the monarch who appointed Sainte-Hermine to the Chamber of Peers after the fall of Napoleon."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOURBON RESTORATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Bourbon Restoration was a period in French history when the Bourbon dynasty returned to power, during which Sainte-Hermine served in the Chamber of Peers."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATHOLIC CHURCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Catholic Church is the religious institution Sainte-Hermine advocated for and served within, both as a priest and a politician."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEINE-ET-OISE DEPARTMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Seine-et-Oise is a department in France where Sainte-Hermine served as Prefect from 1806 to 1813."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHARTER OF 1814&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Charter of 1814 established the constitutional monarchy in France, which Sainte-Hermine supported as a member of the Chamber of Peers."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paris is the city where Sainte-Hermine was responsible for the spiritual well-being of the parish of Saint-Germain-des-Prés."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SAINT-GERMAIN-DES-PRÉS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Saint-Germain-des-Prés is the parish where Sainte-Hermine served as a desservant, despite not holding the official title of parson."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARIE-THÉRÈSE RAVIER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marie-Thérèse Ravier is the author of a 2007 study published in the Journal of French Ecclesiastical History, confirming Sainte-Hermine's position as a desservant."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PIERRE DUPONT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pierre Dupont is the author of a 2012 biography of Sainte-Hermine, published by a French historian, supporting the claim that Sainte-Hermine was a desservant."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATHOLIC HISTORICAL REVIEW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PUBLICATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Catholic Historical Review is a journal that published an article in 2015 noting Sainte-Hermine's unique position as a desservant."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASSEMBLÉE NATIONALE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Assemblée Nationale is the current French parliament, referenced in the context of historical studies about Sainte-Hermine."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENCYCLOPEDIA BRITANNICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PUBLICATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Encyclopedia Britannica is a reference source mentioned in the context of the Girondin faction."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HERMINE.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hermine. is a person mentioned in the text, though no further details are provided about her attributes or activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARCHIVES NATIONALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Archives Nationales is a location, likely referring to a national archives institution."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0383</data>
    </node>
